  "description": "Given an array of unique integers, return the number of binary trees you can make such that each non-leaf node has a value equal to the product of its two children.",
  "target": null,
  "pseudocode": "1. arr.sort((a, b) => a - b)\n2. dp = new Map()\n3. for i from 0 to arr.length - 1:\n4.   dp.set(arr[i], 1)\n5.   for j from 0 to i - 1:\n6.     if arr[i] % arr[j] === 0:\n7.       right = arr[i] / arr[j]\n8.       if dp.has(right):\n9.         dp.set(arr[i], dp.get(arr[i]) + dp.get(arr[j]) * dp.get(right))\n10. return sum(dp.values()) % (10^9 + 7)",
